Short Description

Urgent Change Request - Increase TempDB Data Files from 8 to 20 as per Vendor Recommendation

Description

The application vendor has reviewed the SQL Server performance and recommended increasing the number of TempDB data files from the current 8 files to 20 files on the server. This change has been identified as a priority requirement to improve TempDB workload distribution and prevent potential performance bottlenecks related to TempDB contention.

The change will involve adding additional TempDB data files, aligning file sizes and autogrowth settings, and validating TempDB configuration after implementation. A SQL Server service restart may be required for the changes to take full effect.

Current Configuration: 8 TempDB data files
 Required Configuration: 20 TempDB data files

Symptom
Vendor identified insufficient TempDB data files for the current workload.
Potential TempDB allocation/contention issues may impact application performance.
Recommendation marked as high priority by the vendor and requires immediate implementation to avoid performance degradation.
TempDB configuration is currently below vendor-recommended standards for this environment.
Additional Notes
Vendor Recommendation: Increase TempDB files from 8 to 20.
Priority: High / Urgent.
Business Impact: Potential application and database performance degradation if not addressed promptly.
Implementation Window: Earliest available maintenance window recommended.
